  "status": "completed",
  "output": "The `cd &&` combo is blocked. Rather than fight it, I'll make the script resolve paths relative to its own location — more robust anyway.`compute_norms.py` is written and verified ✅\n\nOutput:\n```\nclient1: 0.8660   (= √0.75)\nclient2: 1.7321   (= √3)\nclient3: 2.0000   (= √4)\n```\n\nA couple of design notes:\n- The script reads `num_clients` from `config.json`, so it automatically picks up new clients if you add `client4.json` etc.\n- Paths resolve relative to the script's own directory, so it runs correctly from anywhere.\n\nWorth noticing: client2 and client3 both exceed the clipping bound of 1.5 — presumably that gets clipped in the aggregation step whenever you're ready.",
